# TypeScript standards (clean + efficient)

- Prefer **explicit types at module boundaries** (exports, public methods); rely on inference internally.
- Keep functions small and single-purpose; avoid “do-everything” methods.
- Avoid dead code, empty statements, stray semicolons, and unused imports/vars.
- Prefer `const`; don’t mutate unless necessary.
- Use early returns to simplify nested conditionals.
- No `any` unless there is no alternative; if used, constrain scope and justify in PR description (not inline narration).
- Handle async flows explicitly:
  - await waits/assertions before interacting
  - avoid arbitrary timeouts; use framework waits/read/assert
- Prefer stable data structures:
  - use `satisfies` for object shape checks (already used in this repo)
  - avoid duplicating string unions; centralize where already established
